        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 78-year-old female patient, who presented to our department on 22/03/2016 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited significant dyspnoea, decreased oxygen saturation, and increased sputum production. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received appropriate intravenous fluids. Her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged on 23/03/2016 with optimised inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. I remain available for any further queries.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
